  "term": "visual environment",
  "definition": "Visual environment refers to the visible features of a place and how they are experienced by people, such as landscape characteristics that shape judgments of attractiveness and distinctiveness. In this source, it means the look of urban coastal roads and waterfront settings as influenced by features like openness and greenery.",
